-- title:
--   Function field of the two-chart model: finite-chart normalisation
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $F$ a field with an $R$-algebra structure, and $j \in F$ a nonzero element. Write $B =$ `chartAlgFin R F j` for the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of the elements of $F$ integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $j$, and $\mathfrak{X} =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the two-chart model, the pushout of the two localisation morphisms `fFin R F j` and `fInf R F j`; assume $\mathfrak{X}$ is integral, and assume `hfrac`, that $F$ is a fraction ring of $B$. The assertion is that there exists a ring isomorphism $\varphi : F \xrightarrow{\sim} \mathfrak{X}$`.functionField` with two properties. First, for every point $y$ of `XFin R F j` $= \operatorname{Spec} B$ and every $b \in B$, the element $\varphi(b)$ is the image in the function field, under the canonical map from the stalk of $\mathfrak{X}$ at the point `(ιFin R F j).base y`, of the germ at that point of the section over the open image of the chart morphism `ιFin R F j` obtained from $b$ by transporting along the inverses of `(ιFin R F j).appIso ⊤` and of the canonical isomorphism $B \cong \Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} B)$. Secondly, for every $r \in R$, $\varphi$ sends the image of $r$ in $F$ to `SemistableModel.baseToFunctionField (toBase R F j) r`, that is, to the germ at the generic point of $\mathfrak{X}$ of the global section coming from $r$ via the structure morphism `toBase R F j` to $\operatorname{Spec} R$.
--
--   This identifies the function field of the two-chart integral model with $F$ itself, pinned so that sections of the finite ($j$-)chart correspond to their germs and constants from the base ring correspond to the base-to-function-field homomorphism; it is the finite-chart half of the chart dictionary used when the model is exhibited as a semistable (or normal proper) model, whose data include exactly such an isomorphism `ffEquiv` together with its compatibility with the base. It is cited in the construction of the full two-chart compatibility statement and in the existence of a normal proper model with prescribed valuation subrings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_exists_ringEquiv_functionField_apply_eq_algebraMap_germ_iotaFin.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_SemistableModel

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry AlgebraicCurve AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel

universe u

theorem AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.exists_ringEquiv_functionField_apply_eq_algebraMap_germ_iotaFin
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (F : Type u) [Field F] [Algebra R F] (j : F) [Fact (j ≠ 0)]
    [IsIntegral (AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j)]
    (hfrac : IsFractionRing ↥(chartAlgFin R F j) F) :
    ∃ φ : F ≃+* (AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j).functionField,
      (∀ (y : ↥(XFin R F j)) (b : ↥(chartAlgFin R F j)),
        φ (b : F) = algebraMap ((AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j).presheaf.stalk ((ιFin R F j).base y)) (AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j).functionField
          (((AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j).presheaf.germ ((ιFin R F j) ''ᵁ ⊤) ((ιFin R F j).base y) ⟨y, trivial, rfl⟩).hom
            (((ιFin R F j).appIso ⊤).inv.hom ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of ↥(chartAlgFin R F j))).inv.hom b)))) ∧
      (∀ r : R, φ (algebraMap R F r) = SemistableModel.baseToFunctionField (toBase R F j) r) := by sorry
